  data: {
    LLM: 'Two players take turns moving their stones on a square grid. Pieces move in all directions (orthogonally, one square or sliding like a rook). Capture is by custodian capture: when an opponent stone is flanked on two opposite sides by your stones, it is captured and removed. Win by capturing all opponent stones or blocking the opponent so they have no legal moves. No random elements; pure strategy.',
    Player: 'Two players take turns moving their stones on a square grid. Pieces move in all directions (orthogonally, one square or sliding like a rook). Capture is by custodian capture: when an opponent stone is flanked on two opposite sides by your stones, it is captured and removed. Win by capturing all opponent stones or blocking the opponent so they have no legal moves. No random elements; pure strategy.',
    objective: 'Capture all opponent stones or block the opponent so they have no legal moves.',
    gameplay: 'Two players take turns moving their stones on a square grid. Pieces move in all directions (orthogonally, one square or sliding like a rook). Capture is by custodian capture: when an opponent stone is flanked on two opposite sides by your stones, it is captured and removed. Win by capturing all opponent stones or blocking the opponent so they have no legal moves. No random elements; pure strategy.',
    keyRules: [
      'Pieces move orthogonally on the board, one square or sliding along a row or column.',
      'Capture by surrounding an opponent piece on two opposite sides (custodian capture).',
      'Win by capturing all opponent pieces or blocking all legal moves.',
      'Keep stones in formation; isolated pieces are vulnerable to pincer capture.',
    ],
